  "headline": "Indonesian Coalition Parties Prepare Vice Presidential Candidates",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesia Coalition Discusses New VP Candidates",
  "metaDescription": "President Prabowo Subianto has given coalition parties one week to submit potential nominees to replace outgoing Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "President Prabowo Subianto requested coalition parties to submit two potential vice presidential nominees within one week.",
    "The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has scheduled the election of a new vice president for December 2, 2026.",
    "An ad hoc verification team consisting of 36 members has been formed by the MPR to oversee the selection process."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political landscape in Indonesia has shifted following the departure of Gibran Rakabuming Raka from his vice-presidential role after two years in office. In response, President Prabowo Subianto has instructed the governing coalition parties to deliberate and propose suitable candidates for the vacancy. The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has moved to formalize the transition by establishing a 36-member ad hoc verification team tasked with managing the selection procedures. While some coalition members, such as PAN, have suggested considering figures from the Gerindra party, others have indicated they will defer to the President's final decision. The official process is gaining momentum as the MPR has designated December 2, 2026, as the date for the parliamentary election to select the new Vice President of Indonesia.",
